// The frontier cast - spliced into default.amd's `## Lifeforms` section. A lifeform
// with no Host is a galaxy-wide comms NPC (hailable with no target selected). Face
// is a keyword (terran / male / female) or a literal face string; Scene names the
// dialogue scene that is this character's voice.

# [Frontier Command](frontier_command)
---
Face: terran
Roles: tsn, command
Scene: frontier_hail
Color: #4cf
---
Distant TSN fleet command, keeping a thin watch over the frontier.

// An authored named passenger (delivery B): a lifeform with a Pickup + Deliver to
// + Pays. Offered for transport at her pickup station; boards your ship on accept
// and disembarks (with the fare) on reaching her destination. She has a voice too.
//
// `Patience:` makes her WAIT rather than sit on a menu forever - she is spawned on
// her pickup station and asks, more insistently as her window closes, and leaves if
// nobody comes. The clock is a station-held quest; the urges below are only its
// voice, which is why they declare no stakes of their own.
# [Doctor Sela Voss](sela_voss)
---
Face: female
Roles: civilian
Pickup: 0, 0
Deliver to: -5, 3
Reward: 500 credits
Patience: 20m
Scene: sela_hail
Color: #6cf
---
A xenobiologist needing passage from the home base to the Verdant worlds.

// The stage count IS the curve: `%` while there is time, `%%` as it runs short,
// `%%%` at the end. `Escalates: with deadline` reads her Patience clock, so the
// tempo is set by the number above and nothing here has to agree with it.
## [Still waiting for passage](sela_waiting)
---
Urge
Every: 4m
Escalates: with deadline
---
% Doctor Voss is on the docking ring, if anyone is bound for the Verdant worlds.
% Sela Voss here - still looking for passage out to Verdant. I can pay.
%% Voss again. My window at the Verdant site closes, captain.
%% I am asking around the ring now. Anyone headed out that way?
%%% Last call. I need to be on a hull today or not at all.

// Weight 90 outranks the global speech floor - someone leaving for good should not
// be swallowed because another voice spoke five seconds ago. `self` is her, so no
// role has to be invented just to let this line point at the person saying it.
## [Gives up and goes](sela_gives_up)
---
Urge
Whenever: quest waiting_sela_voss failed
Weight: 90
Action:
  - self departs
---
% Never mind. I have found other arrangements.
% Too late, I am afraid. I have taken a berth on a freighter.

// A saboteur passenger (delivery + slice 3): a lifeform with a Sabotage list. Pays
// suspiciously well; once aboard he damages those ship systems one at a time (crew
// raise the alarm) until you hail and Detain him.
# [A Nervous Courier](courier)
---
Face: male
Roles: civilian
Pickup: 6, 4
Deliver to: 0, 0
Reward: 600 credits
Sabotage: sensors, weapons, engines
Scene: courier_hail
Color: #f84
---
A twitchy courier with a heavy sealed case, paying well for fast, quiet passage off
the Iron Concord home. Too well.
